  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115576",
      "title": "Extending Built-in Elements with Custom Components via Attribute Selectors",
      "lectureOrder": 106,
      "videoOrder": 100,
      "sourceHash": "5e3fc2d803463d59cd539c414ad11d9a09c3c2cc0707bd2e341dcea5feda6bb8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 1.283,
          "en": "So here I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.283,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "to extend the built-in button.component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 5.22,
          "en": "And as mentioned, if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 5.22,
          "end": 8.76,
          "en": "if you wanna essentially extend a built-in component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.76,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "you can do that in a slightly different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 12.513,
          "en": "than you did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "Instead of putting that button element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "into the template of our button.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "we could focus on just having the actual content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 25.353,
          "en": "of the button in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "And we could then go to the button.component TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "and change the selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "because this selector here is not restricted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "to being an element selector as we have it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "and as we had it in all our other components thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 45.57,
          "en": "Indeed, it's the most common case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.57,
          "end": 48.51,
          "en": "and it's typically the best choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.51,
          "end": 50.79,
          "en": "to have an element selector like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.34,
          "en": "but you're not limited to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.34,
          "end": 58.34,
          "en": "Instead, Angular supports other kinds of selectors as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60,
          "en": "And attached, you find a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "to the official documentation about component selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "where you can learn all about the different kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 70.563,
          "en": "of selectors that could be used with Angular components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "And one kind of selector you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 78.86,
          "en": "is an attribute selector instead of an element selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.38,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "An element selector is always defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "by just putting the element name here, like button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 87.357,
          "en": "or typically prefixed with app-.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "An attribute selector, on the other hand, is defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 94.22999999999999,
          "en": "by using square brackets here, which has nothing to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "with property binding or anything like that in this place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "Instead, this is just how in CSS you would set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "an attribute selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.28,
          "en": "and the component selector from @Component works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "like a CSS selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 111.12,
          "en": "And then you can set up any attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.12,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "of your choice like appButton,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "which, of course, isn't a built-in attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "but now whenever you would add that attribute to an element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "this component would become active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 126.663,
          "en": "and would effectively replace it or take control of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "And you can even combine that with other selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.8,
          "en": "For example, if I write button[appButton],",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.8,
          "end": 135.22899999999998,
          "en": "I am telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.22899999999998,
          "end": 139.71,
          "en": "that any button element anywhere in my application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "that also has the appButton attribute on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.473,
          "en": "should be controlled by this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.09,
          "end": 149.25,
          "en": "Besides the attribute selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.25,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "you can, by the way, also, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "use a CSS class selector by adding a dot at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 158.34,
          "en": "and you can also combine that to control buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 160.44299999999998,
          "en": "that have a class of button on them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "But here I wanna control buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 167.57999999999998,
          "en": "that have the attribute appButton on them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.57999999999998,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "and it's considered a good practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 174.32999999999998,
          "en": "to prefix your custom attributes that are meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.32999999999998,
          "end": 178.2,
          "en": "to be used by Angular with your application prefix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 180.93,
          "en": "So the same prefix you, for example, used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.93,
          "end": 182.493,
          "en": "for all your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "And that's therefore now the selector I wanna have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 190.293,
          "en": "for this button.component to extend that built-in button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.18,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "Now, if I now wanna use that component, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "in the header.component, I do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 200.643,
          "en": "by bringing back the regular built-in button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.54,
          "end": 205.18,
          "en": "but by now also placing appButton as a attribute on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 210.063,
          "en": "or whichever attribute you chose in your component selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.49,
          "end": 213.84,
          "en": "Now, I don't need to enter anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.84,
          "end": 215.34,
          "en": "between the button tags here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.34,
          "end": 217.71,
          "en": "because right now, here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 218.97,
          "en": "I have all the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.97,
          "end": 222.48,
          "en": "that should be output here in the button component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.48,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "and it is that template that will now be rendered by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 228.75,
          "en": "for this button component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.75,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "because we are now taking control of this built-in button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 235.2,
          "en": "with our custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.2,
          "end": 239.19,
          "en": "And that can be a pretty powerful Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.19,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "and pattern because it essentially allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "to use built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 247.95,
          "en": "and extend their functionality or templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 249.87,
          "en": "So with that, if I now saved it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.87,
          "end": 253.89,
          "en": "and I reload, I still have my logout button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.89,
          "end": 255.9,
          "en": "but if we now inspect that, you see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.9,
          "end": 260.79,
          "en": "that now the app-button wrapper around it is gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.79,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "and instead now it's the built-in button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 265.89,
          "en": "that's being rendered, but our template is then rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.89,
          "end": 266.733,
          "en": "inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 271.92,
          "en": "and that saves us this extra unnecessary DOM element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.92,
          "end": 273.873,
          "en": "that we had in the DOM before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.95,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "Now, you could use that on other components as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 281.34000000000003,
          "en": "but typically, this pattern of selecting an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.34000000000003,
          "end": 286.17,
          "en": "by attribute is used if you wanna extend a built-in element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.17,
          "end": 289.17,
          "en": "Whenever you're building a brand new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.17,
          "end": 292.23,
          "en": "that just wraps a bunch of built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.23,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "but doesn't really replace one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 298.98,
          "en": "you should use the element selector as we did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.98,
          "end": 300.84,
          "en": "So that should be your default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.84,
          "end": 302.97,
          "en": "but knowing about this kind of selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.97,
          "end": 306.393,
          "en": "and that you can do that with Angular is important.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
